Today is Sunday.
It is morning time.
My neighborhood is very quiet.
I go to a corner shop.
There is one shopkeeper there.
I call him 'Dada'.
There are very colorful sweets in his shop.
I buy one box of sweets.
I give Dada two hundred rupees.
I look at a photo on my phone.
Dada asks, "Madam, who is in your photo?"
I smile and say, "That is my family."
My family lives in Mexico.
Today I have a video call with them.
I am going to show them these Indian sweets.
I take the sweet box in my hand.
I go back to my room happily.
